# {{.Title}}

An API built with [Gonestly](https://yaboylino.github.io/gonestly-docs).

## Development

```sh
gonestly dev
```

This starts the API on http://localhost:3000 and restarts it on every change. The
documentation is served at http://localhost:3000/docs.

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `gonestly dev` | Runs the API and rebuilds it on every change |
| `gonestly generate resource <name>` | Adds a complete resource with routes, service and table |
| `gonestly routes` | Lists every route |
| `go test ./...` | Runs the tests |
| `make fmt` | Formats the code with gofmt |
{{- if .Database}}
| `gonestly migrate create <name>` | Adds a migration |
| `gonestly migrate status` | Shows which migrations are applied |
{{- end}}

Settings are read from environment variables and the `.env` file; see `.env.example`.

Go code is indented with tabs, shown four wide: `.editorconfig` and `.vscode/settings.json` set that up and
format on save. In GoLand, turn on "Reformat code" under Settings, Tools, Actions on Save.
